-- infra/e2e/seed/60-phase2-batch3-fixture.sql.tmpl
--
-- Phase 2 batch 3 (mig-infra) — data-point parity fixture for the SIX new
-- page-pairs this batch covers: /crm-dashboard-advanced, /system-status,
-- /templates, /groups, /line-groups, /line-group-detail. Applied AFTER
-- 30-phase2-batch1-fixture.sql.tmpl and 40-phase2-batch2-fixture.sql.tmpl
-- (already piped into the SAME app/tenant DB by parity.mjs's
-- seedDatabase()) — additive only, same pattern 40-* used on top of 30-*
-- (see that file's own header comment for the precedent). Does not touch
-- any table those two files already seed (users/messages/orders/
-- transactions/user_tags/activity_logs/broadcasts/customer_segments/
-- auto_replies/user_behaviors) — this file only INSERTs into tables no
-- earlier batch has touched: templates, groups, user_groups, line_groups,
-- line_group_members, line_group_messages.
--
-- No USE statement of its own — same convention as 20-/30-/40-: the caller
-- (parity.mjs's seedDatabase()) prepends `USE \`<app-db>\`;`.
--
-- DETERMINISM: every timestamp is a MySQL relative-date expression
-- (NOW()/DATE_SUB(NOW(), INTERVAL n DAY|HOUR)), never a wall-clock literal —
-- same reasoning as 30-*/40-*'s own header comments.
--
-- ===========================================================================
-- WHY NO `line_accounts` ROWS (still true for this batch — read before
-- adding any). Full mechanical trace lives in
-- 40-phase2-batch2-fixture.sql.tmpl's own header comment (includes/header.php
-- lines 138-172, classes/AdminAuth.php::getAccessibleBots(),
-- packages/auth/src/session.ts) — not repeated verbatim here. Summary as it
-- applies to THIS batch's two $currentBotId-touching pages, decided jointly
-- with mig-ui (both pagesA and pagesB) per this batch's brief and written up
-- in docs/runbooks/phase2-batch1-users-dashboard-parity.md's "Phase 2 batch
-- 3" section:
--
--   - groups.php (line 11: `require_once 'includes/header.php';` BEFORE any
--     of its own queries) inherits header.php's sticky auto-selected
--     `$currentBotId`. Seeding even one `is_active=1` line_accounts row would
--     re-trigger that auto-select on parity.mjs's ONE shared phpSid session —
--     silently re-scoping every EARLIER batch's already-passing
--     line_account_id-sensitive query (batch 1's dashboard/crm.php,
--     batch 2's analytics tabs) for the REST of the run, per the exact
--     hazard batch 2's file already reasoned through. Still not worth
--     re-triggering just to populate groups.php's `getAllUsersForGroups()`
--     dropdown with a non-null bot scope — that query's `(line_account_id =
--     ? OR line_account_id IS NULL)` single-bind pattern already resolves to
--     "match every line_account_id IS NULL row" when $currentBotId is null,
--     which is exactly what every batch 1/2/3 user row is. Decision: NO.
--   - line-groups.php (line 15: `$currentBotId = $_SESSION['current_bot_id']
--     ?? null;`, its OWN local read, BEFORE `require_once
--     'includes/header.php'` on line 130 — confirmed by reading the full
--     file) never even reaches header.php's auto-select before running its
--     own queries, and no page in this harness's fixture ever sets
--     `$_SESSION['current_bot_id']` (no `?switch_bot=` fetch, no active
--     line_accounts row for header.php to auto-select from on ANY earlier
--     page fetch either) — so `$currentBotId` is null here regardless.
--     Seeding a line_accounts row would ALSO risk retroactively feeding
--     header.php's auto-select on some earlier page in the shared session.
--     Decision: NO, same as groups.php.
--
--   Net effect (verified against the tenant template's own schema, not
--   guessed): `line_groups.line_account_id` is NOT NULL (no DEFAULT) but has
--   NO enforced FOREIGN KEY to `line_accounts` — every line_groups row below
--   uses a SYNTHETIC id (9001/9002) that matches NO row in the (empty)
--   `line_accounts` table. `line-groups.php`'s LEFT JOIN renders
--   `bot_name = NULL` -> PHP's `htmlspecialchars($group['bot_name'] ?? '-')`
--   -> literal "-", a deterministic, fully-comparable state on both stacks
--   (see extractLineGroupsPage's own doc in infra/e2e/lib/extract.mjs).
--   `line_group_members.line_account_id` / `line_group_messages.
--   line_account_id` are NOT NULL DEFAULT 1 — neither line-group-detail.php
--   nor its Next port ever filters by line_account_id on these two tables
--   (grepped both — WHERE clauses are `group_id = ?` only), so the exact
--   synthetic value is inert; set to the owning group's own synthetic id
--   (9001) purely for fixture readability, not because anything reads it.
-- ===========================================================================

